      {
        "id": 126132,
        "name": "seesome",
        "username": "seesome",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/{size}/2018_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-20T18:18:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My problem with Gotham is that it's painfully grim, grimy, and glum (which makes sense for Gotham city but not fun television viewing for me). &nbsp;Also, the storyline&nbsp;<span>makes very little sense if you try to work it into existing Batman mythology - which is fine for a TV show, but makes it less fun for me.</span></p><p>Flash &amp; Arrow OTOH, are clearly written by fans and they fill the shows to the brim with nods to other characters and creators. &nbsp;But they mostly do it through background referenes so as to not make it annoying to non-fans (so says my wife, who's barely read any DC comics, but really enjoys the shows).</p><p>Flash and Arrow mess with the original stories as well, but they don't throw out the source material.</p>",
